# xv6-riscv Extended: Muhammad Owais (Memory Management)

**Course:** Operating Systems / Computer System Architecture
* *Instructor:** Sir Raza
**Group:** <Muhammad Owais>, <Muhammad Shoaib>, <Muhammad Mudassir>
**Base:** https://github.com/mit-pdos/xv6-riscv (base commit: <hash>)

## 1. Overview
This repo contains Member B's part of the group semester project. It extends
the xv6-riscv memory management with lazy allocation, mmap, copy-on-write
fork, and 2 MB superpages. The other members work in their own repos
(Member A: scheduling/syscalls/perf counters; Member C: file system/cache/multicore).
All three are merged in the final integrated repo: <link>.

## 2. My Modules

| ID | Module | Description | Difficulty |
|----|--------|-------------|-----------|
| OS-3a | Lazy allocation | `sbrk` only grows the address space; pages are allocated on first access via page fault | Medium |
| OS-2 | Copy-on-Write fork | Parent and child share pages read-only; a write fault copies the page; reference counting in `kalloc.c` | Hard |
| OS-3b | mmap / munmap | Per-process VMA table; files are mapped into memory and loaded on page fault; dirty pages written back for MAP_SHARED | Hard |
| ARCH-3 | Superpages (2 MB) | Level-1 leaf PTEs in the Sv39 page table to reduce page walks and TLB pressure | Hard |

## 3. Files Modified
| Module | Files |
|--------|-------|
| OS-3a | `kernel/sysproc.c`, `kernel/trap.c`, `kernel/vm.c` |
| OS-2 | `kernel/vm.c`, `kernel/kalloc.c`, `kernel/trap.c`, `kernel/riscv.h` |
| OS-3b | `kernel/sysfile.c`, `kernel/proc.h`, `kernel/proc.c`, `kernel/trap.c`, `kernel/syscall.*` |
| ARCH-3 | `kernel/vm.c`, `kernel/kalloc.c`, `kernel/riscv.h` |

